# BUG: z is assigned only inside "if x == 3", so outside that branch it should not exist.
# It does. A variable's first assignment ignores whether its branch was taken, so z is 1 for
# every x, the test below never fires, and the program is satisfied by all 256 messages.
# The constraint evaporates: this file reports "More than 5 consistent timelines" when the
# question it asks has exactly one answer, x = 3 (see branch_leak_fixed.px).
bits 8
x = future(x)
if x == 3:
    z = 1
if z == 0:
    x = x + 1
show x
